/ A run saved inside a bound call keeps %!event%: Log is bound before each goal, so it runs before Work starts, saves the
/ run there and keeps it in workspace/run.plang. Resumed, the run goes on from that save inside Log and reads
/ %!event!item.name% right after it — no goal starts in between — so it names the goal the saved event fired for. The
/ marker, written after the save and never in the snapshot, says the run is the resumed one; the resumed run then goes on
/ through this goal and ends at the marker.
Start
- before each goal, call Log
- call Work
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - end goal
- write "here" to file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- read file 'workspace/run.plang', write to %snapshot%
- resume %snapshot%
- read file 'workspace/seen.txt', write to %seen%
- assert %seen% equals "Work"
- delete file 'workspace/run.plang'
- delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- delete file 'workspace/seen.txt'

/ The goal the event fires for.
Work
- set %worked% = "yes"

/ The bound call: saves the run while it runs; resumed, it writes what the event fired for.
Log
- save snapshot, write to %run%
- save %run% to file 'workspace/run.plang'
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - write "%!event!item.name%" to file 'workspace/seen.txt'
